Lab 20: Comprehensive Review: Building and Managing a Project
Objectives
By the end of this lab, students will be able to:

Create and manage a well-organized Ansible inventory for a multi-node environment
Develop modular Ansible roles for common, web server, and database server configuration
Build a master playbook that orchestrates deployment across multiple host groups
Debug and troubleshoot playbook execution using check mode, verbosity flags, and ad hoc commands
Apply best practices for structuring a production-style Ansible project
Prerequisites
Before starting this lab, students should have:

Basic understanding of Linux command line operations
Familiarity with YAML syntax and structure
Knowledge of Ansible fundamentals (inventories, playbooks, modules)
Experience with Ansible roles and variables
Understanding of SSH key-based authentication
Text editor proficiency (vim, nano, or similar)
Required tooling (install on the control node if not already present):

sudo apt update
sudo apt install -y ansible sshpass
ansible --version
